    <categoryEntry name="High Command" id="94e3-ff49-273a-5079" hidden="false">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Heavenly Commander" id="35d5-8b9c-9acf-c610" hidden="false" typeId="fe4c-5b77-ab77-e578" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="5cee-5283-c95d-c323">While this unit is present on the battlefield (including if it is embarked within Transport), you may select any of the abilities from the Divine Mandates ability to use whenever their description states they can be used.

Additionally, while this model is not destroyed, your Force Rule is active.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="5cee-5283-c95d-c323" join="

" type="append" value="**Frontline Assault Force:**

When a unit in your army performs an Advance move, if the result of that Advance roll is less than 4, that unit may shoot or charge this turn. Additionally, if a unit Remained Stationary, they receive an improvement of 1 to their Save Roll characteristic (to a maximum of 3+).">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="06fc-0e49-5845-7f3d" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
            <modifier field="5cee-5283-c95d-c323" join="

" type="append" value="**Psychological Warfare Division:**

All Horde Units receive Feel No Pain 4+.">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="f8e2-61a3-1fea-ccb2" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Divine Mandates" id="2c68-47a9-247e-7e28" hidden="false" typeId="1b5f-730f-9148-226b" typeName="Divine Mandates">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="3d14-93cc-4e82-9d0e">While this unit is present on the battlefield (including if it is embarked within Transport), you may select any of the following abilities to use whenever their description states they can be used.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="3d14-93cc-4e82-9d0e" join="

" type="append" value="**Frontline Assault Force**

Back to the Front (1 MP) - 
WHEN: Any phase during your turn except for your Command Phase.
TARGET: Any War Dogs Infantry Unit within 18&quot; of your High Command unit.
EFFECT: The target unit may make a normal move of D6+2&quot; in any direction. The range of that movement cannot exceed the Movement characteristic of the target unit.
RESTRICTIONS: The target unit cannot be within, or end a move within, Engagement Range of an enemy unit.


Lay Suppressing Fire (1 MP) - 
WHEN: Start of your Shooting Phase
TARGET: Any visible Enemy Unit within 12&quot; of your High Command unit
EFFECT: Until the end of your turn, the next time that unit is targeted by one of your units with an attack made by Ranged Weapons, if one or more attacks made by that unit were successful, that enemy unit receives SHOCK until the end of their turn.
RESTRICTIONS: The target unit cannot be within Engagement Range of a friendly unit.


Flank and Surround (1 MP) - 
When: The Reinforcements step of the Enemy Movement Phase
TARGET: One friendly unit within Strategic Reserves
EFFECT: That unit can arrive on the battlefield as if it were the Reinforcements step of your Movement phase, and if every model in that unit has the Deep Strike ability, you can set that unit up as described in the Deep Strike ability (even though it is not your Movement phase).
RESTRICTIONS: You cannot use this Stratagem to enable a unit to arrive on the battlefield during a battle round it would not normally be able to do so in.


Call for Reinforcements (1 MP) -
When: Any phase
TARGET: One War Dogs Infantry unit from your army that was just destroyed. You can target that unit with this Stratagem even though it was just destroyed.
EFFECT: Add a new unit to your army identical to your destroyed unit, in Strategic Reserves, at its Starting Strength and with all of its wounds remaining.
RESTRICTIONS: When adding a new unit, do not add any Attached Character models, only the base unit.
">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="06fc-0e49-5845-7f3d" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule name="If He Deems It So..." id="389e-f30d-3003-b483" hidden="false">
          <description>At the start of any phase during your turn, if you do not already have a Chosen Apostate selected, select one enemy unit visible to a friendly High Command/Command Character Unit in your army, that unit is your Chosen Apostate. Until that enemy unit is destroyed, friendly units targeting your Chosen Apostate may reroll missed hit rolls of 1 and missed wound rolls of 1 when targeting that unit. As soon as that enemy unit is destroyed, you may select another enemy unit to be your Chosen Apostate.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </categoryEntry>
