      <profiles>
        <profile name="Ars Moriendi" id="276d-0df9-26e0-b375" hidden="false" typeId="fe4c-5b77-ab77-e578" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="5cee-5283-c95d-c323">When a model in the bearer&apos;s unit is about to be destroyed as a result of an enemy attack, you may select one of the following Death Rites to apply to the bearer&apos;s unit. An individual Priest model may only perform each Death Rite once per battle.

**Abandon Despair** - Remove the destroyed model from this unit. This unit receives the GLEE status for one battle round.

**Embrace Redemption** - Before removing the target model from this unit, roll a D3. On a 1, do remove that model. On a 2, do not remove that model, and return another destroyed model to this unit. On a 3, do not remove that model and return 2 other destroyed models to this unit.

**Harness Faith** - If this unit is not in Engagement Range of an enemy unit, after removing the destroyed model from this unit, this unit may perform an attack with one of its Ranged Weapon profiles against the unit whose attacks destroyed the target model.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry name="Priest" id="a512-8dee-22a9-6a3d" hidden="false" import="true" type="model">
